WEBVTT

1
00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:17.250
Hi. My name is Peter Parker.

2
00:01:19.333 --> 00:01:22.167
You don't remember me.
but I have something to tell you...

3
00:01:22.417 --> 00:01:24.333
that's gonna sound crazy.

4
00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:28.333
But it's the truth.

5
00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:32.000
And I know you're gonna believe me...

6
00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:35.250
because you're very good
at telling when I'm lying.

7
00:01:37.083 --> 00:01:39.417
E.V.. can you check the calibration
of my targeting matrix?

8
00:01:39.583 --> 00:01:41.167
That doesn't feel zeroed in to me.

9
00:01:41.333 --> 00:01:43.333
Checking target calibration.

10
00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:53.333
Hey. E.V.. take five.

11
00:01:54.083 --> 00:01:55.083
Standing by.

12
00:02:00.833 --> 00:02:02.250
We used to know each other.

13
00:02:03.667 --> 00:02:05.417
We were together.

14
00:02:06.667 --> 00:02:08.167
But something bad was gonna happen...

15
00:02:08.333 --> 00:02:11.833
and the only way to stop it
was to make everyone forget me

16
00:02:16.833 --> 00:02:18.917
First day at MIT. let's go!

17
00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:21.250
Oh. my gosh! We're here! We made it!

18
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.000
MJ. come on.

19
00:02:23.167 --> 00:02:24.167
Including you.

20
00:02:24.333 --> 00:02:25.583
Pretend like you're not the happiest
you've ever been...

21
00:02:25.833 --> 00:02:27.167
in your entire life right now.

22
00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:29.083
I can't.

23
00:02:29.333 --> 00:02:32.000
-Let's just do this! You're happy!
-Okay. okay. okay. Okay.

24
00:02:32.167 --> 00:02:34.167
Because I'm not just Peter Parker.

25
00:02:35.917 --> 00:02:37.167
I'm Spider-Man.

26
00:02:37.333 --> 00:02:40.500
I'm really. really understanding the culture
out here in Boston is just so different.

27
00:02:40.667 --> 00:02:43.417
And sometimes
Spider-Man has to do the hard thing...

28
00:02:43.583 --> 00:02:45.500
even if it breaks Peter Parker's heart.

29
00:02:45.667 --> 00:02:48.833
And everyone here is like.
"Pahk the cah by the hahba."

30
00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:52.083
And maybe that's my responsibility.

31
00:02:53.333 --> 00:02:54.750
To live alone with the truth.

32
00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:59.750
But the truth is. MJ. that I love you.

33
00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:02.250
And I hope that deep down...

34
00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:05.083
something inside of you
remembers that you love me. too.

35
00:03:06.583 --> 00:03:09.167
Suspect is 5'8". 5'10". medium build.

36
00:03:09.333 --> 00:03:12.083
But until then. I'm just gonna be Spider-Man.

37
00:03:18.083 --> 00:03:19.167
Incoming!

38
00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:23.500
Hey. get him!

39
00:03:24.917 --> 00:03:26.250
Hey. hey. hey. Whoa. whoa. whoa!

40
00:03:39.250 --> 00:03:41.167
Members of the Manfredi crime syndicate...

41
00:03:41.333 --> 00:03:42.833
were apprehended by Spider-Man yesterday.

42
00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:05.250
Hey. we live on the same floor.

43
00:04:07.333 --> 00:04:08.250
Cool.

44
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.500
Does anybody ever come up here?

45
00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:16.250
Not unless they like asbestos.

46
00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:19.500
We've just been using it for storage.

47
00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:21.917
It's perfect.

48
00:04:23.417 --> 00:04:25.917
Hey. everyone. sophomore-year-Ned is back.

49
00:04:26.417 --> 00:04:29.167
Older. wiser. flyer.

50
00:04:30.417 --> 00:04:31.250
Let's go!

51
00:04:32.083 --> 00:04:34.500
-What is on your face?
Little Caesars -How do you feel about it?

52
00:04:34.667 --> 00:04:36.583
I mean. you look
like an assistant coach.

53
00:04:36.833 --> 00:04:37.750
Huh.

54
00:04:41.333 --> 00:04:43.083
You sure you wanna do this. Scorpion?

55
00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:44.667
Did you miss me. Spidey?

56
00:04:50.833 --> 00:04:52.000
If I drop you from here...

57
00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:54.500
how long you think
it will take you to hit the ground?

58
00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:56.917
Well. I don't know. You tell me.

59
00:04:58.333 --> 00:04:59.500
Let's end this on a high note. huh?

60
00:05:05.833 --> 00:05:06.917
Yo. Lonnie!

61
00:05:07.583 --> 00:05:08.583
Wha ha happened?

62
00:05:08.833 --> 00:05:12.250
DeWolff. all the evidence you're gonna need
is in the trunk of his car.

63
00:05:12.417 --> 00:05:14.417
You tryin' to take my job. Spider-Man?

64
00:05:14.667 --> 00:05:16.917
Hey. you guys are the professionals.
I'm just a volunteer.

65
00:05:27.417 --> 00:05:29.417
It's a new New York.

66
00:05:29.583 --> 00:05:33.083
Thanks to Spider-Man.
crime rates have dropped to a record low.

67
00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.417
Police and Damage Control
give much of the credit...

68
00:05:35.583 --> 00:05:36.583
to the masked hero.

69
00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:38.000
Initiate HUD test.

70
00:05:38.167 --> 00:05:40.000
Armed robbery at Civic Union Bank.

71
00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:42.167
In the past six months.
he has taken down...

72
00:05:42.333 --> 00:05:45.167
every major crime lord
across the five boroughs...

73
00:05:45.417 --> 00:05:48.833
including the superpowered
ninja group The Hand.

74
00:05:52.750 --> 00:05:54.917
He is the pride of New York City.

75
00:05:55.083 --> 00:05:58.667
The hero every grown-up relies on
and every kid wants to be.

76
00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:02.000
Final semester. MIT.

77
00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:04.500
Oh. my gosh. we're graduating in a month.

78
00:06:04.917 --> 00:06:08.167
We've made so many memories.
Where do I begin?

79
00:06:08.333 --> 00:06:11.250
Night swimming in the Charles River
with Jim and Wiley.

80
00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:14.167
The infamous food fun at the Banana Lounge.

81
00:06:14.417 --> 00:06:18.583
Pulling all-nighters in Stud 5
with MJ and Nate Dawg.

82
00:06:18.833 --> 00:06:21.500
It feels like yesterday
I was sitting on a roof with MJ...

83
00:06:21.667 --> 00:06:24.750
dreaming about coming here together.
and I still can't believe we did it.

84
00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.500
I'm so grateful
for all the friends that I've made.

85
00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:30.000
I couldn't imagine
going through this with anyone else.

86
00:06:30.167 --> 00:06:32.000
Ned. who do you think
is actually watching these?

87
00:06:32.333 --> 00:06:34.667
-I don't know. But maybe someone.
-Okay.

88
00:06:34.917 --> 00:06:36.000
Okay. well. bye. someone.

89
00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:38.333
-What? No!
-Bye. We're done. Yeah. we're done.

90
00:06:48.833 --> 00:06:50.750
Leave it outside the door.

91
00:06:55.917 --> 00:06:59.000
I mean. we're talking about downtown Brooklyn. in broad daylight.

92
00:06:59.167 --> 00:07:00.667
High profile job like that.

93
00:07:00.767 --> 00:07:01.917
you know that Foswell was involved.

94
00:07:02.167 --> 00:07:04.250
Yeah. I hear you. but can you prove it?

95
00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:06.167
Yeah. I'm going through
his financial records...

96
00:07:06.417 --> 00:07:07.833
and I'm following his crew every night.

97
00:07:08.833 --> 00:07:10.750
Do you do anything besides work?

98
00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:12.417
You know the saying.
"You do something you love...

99
00:07:12.583 --> 00:07:13.833
you don't work a day in your life."

100
00:07:15.417 --> 00:07:17.333
-Mom. where's my calculator?
-I don't know.

101
00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:21.250
Trust me. aight?
Being married to the job never ends well.

102
00:07:21.583 --> 00:07:23.417
Well. don't worry about it. I'll be okay.

103
00:07:23.667 --> 00:07:26.250
Oh. yeah?
You still getting them headaches. though?

104
00:07:27.667 --> 00:07:30.000
Yeah. But I'll be fine.

105
00:07:30.167 --> 00:07:31.250
I don't know. man.

106
00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:33.417
I think you're body's tryin'
to tell you somethin'.

107
00:07:33.667 --> 00:07:35.833
Like you need to get outta that suit
every once in a while.

108
00:07:36.083 --> 00:07:37.833
Mom. do you know where my calculator is?

109
00:07:38.083 --> 00:07:39.000
I don't know. Papi.

110
00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:42.250
What you need is some real human connection.

111
00:07:42.500 --> 00:07:43.667
What? And we're not connecting?

112
00:07:44.083 --> 00:07:48.750
Nah. dude. I don't know your name.
your face. or nothing about you.

113
00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:51.167
I don't think you've ever asked me a question
about my life.

114
00:07:51.333 --> 00:07:52.333
Sure. I have.

115
00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:53.750
Yeah. what are my kids' names?

116
00:07:54.417 --> 00:07:56.417
Well. for starters. your son's name's Papi.

117
00:07:58.167 --> 00:07:59.083
Is it Spider-Man?

118
00:07:59.333 --> 00:08:01.250
I can't tell you that. sweetheart.

119
00:08:01.667 --> 00:08:03.083
That means it's Spider-Man.

120
00:08:03.333 --> 00:08:04.333
Gosh.

121
00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:09.833
A hijacked tank is heading southbound
past 34th Street.

122
00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:11.417
All available units respond.

123
00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:12.750
Hey. you getting this?

124
00:08:12.917 --> 00:08:14.583
More work. Lucky you.

125
00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:15.750
Okay. I'll see you out there.

126
00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:17.083
I'm so sorry. I gotta go.

127
00:09:34.417 --> 00:09:35.583
I got you. Spidey!

128
00:09:35.750 --> 00:09:37.083
No. no. I don't need your...

129
00:09:51.417 --> 00:09:52.417
Hey! Heads up!

130
00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:57.417
You okay. kid? Yeah. you're okay.
See ya later.

131
00:10:02.083 --> 00:10:03.417
You wouldn't know it just by looking at it...

132
00:10:03.667 --> 00:10:06.667
but this very street was completely destroyed
in the Battle of New York.

133
00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:16.667
Come on. come on. come on.

134
00:10:18.333 --> 00:10:20.167
Come on.

135
00:10:33.167 --> 00:10:34.083
Oh. God.

136
00:10:42.833 --> 00:10:43.833
Come on.

137
00:10:44.667 --> 00:10:45.250
Hey.

138
00:10:46.833 --> 00:10:48.750
The hell. Frank?
You just hit me with the van!

139
00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:50.167
Quit your whimpering.

140
00:10:50.333 --> 00:10:51.667
We're not doing that again. Frank.

141
00:10:51.833 --> 00:10:53.167
You're goddamn right we're not.

142
00:10:53.333 --> 00:10:55.083
This time you're gonna
get the hell outta my way.

143
00:10:55.583 --> 00:10:57.083
You mean. instead of saving your life?

144
00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:00.417
You gonna talk about
that Staten Island bullshit again?

145
00:11:00.667 --> 00:11:02.000
Well. you said it. not me.

146
00:11:02.167 --> 00:11:03.000
Jeez.

147
00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:05.083
Look. man. you can't just shoot yourself
out of every situation.

148
00:11:05.333 --> 00:11:06.583
Innocent people get hurt.

149
00:11:06.833 --> 00:11:09.167
Who do you think's downrange of that tank.
dumb-dumb?

150
00:11:14.667 --> 00:11:15.667
Suit yourself.

151
00:11:19.333 --> 00:11:20.333
Jackass.

152
00:11:21.333 --> 00:11:22.500
This freakin' guy.

153
00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:39.750
Go home. Frank!

154
00:11:44.417 --> 00:11:45.917
I'm gonna kill this kid.

155
00:11:50.750 --> 00:11:53.000
-DeWolff?
-Are you gonna stop that thing or what?

156
00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:55.583
It's heading straight
for the Damage Control Detention Center.

157
00:11:55.833 --> 00:11:56.750
I'm trying.

158
00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:57.833
Try harder.

159
00:11:58.000 --> 00:11:59.667
There's a lot of scary dudes
locked up in there.

160
00:11:59.833 --> 00:12:01.417
Well. who do you think put them in there?

161
00:12:02.333 --> 00:12:05.583
Let's go. Scorpion. Moving day.

162
00:12:35.833 --> 00:12:38.583
All right. everybody. clear out!
This guy is armed and dangerous.

163
00:12:50.833 --> 00:12:52.333
Get out of the vehicle. ma'am.

164
00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:54.750
I was thinking the same thing.

165
00:13:03.583 --> 00:13:05.000
Spider-Man?

166
00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:07.500
Where am I?

167
00:13:14.667 --> 00:13:15.750
What?

168
00:13:18.333 --> 00:13:19.750
Move! Move! Move!

169
00:13:19.917 --> 00:13:21.667
Keep her for questioning.
Clear the building.

170
00:13:24.833 --> 00:13:26.833
Enjoy the ride. Scorpion!

171
00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:29.500
You won't be seeing much daylight
in supermax.

172
00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:32.500
Scorpions are nocturnal. buddy.

173
00:13:35.583 --> 00:13:38.750
The building is under attack.
Get the prisoner out of here now!

174
00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:44.917
Sir!

175
00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:05.167
You gotta take off now!

176
00:14:05.333 --> 00:14:07.333
The building has been breached. Go! Go!

177
00:14:07.750 --> 00:14:10.333
Hey. fire it up! Go! Go!

178
00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:19.917
Change of plans!

179
00:14:20.583 --> 00:14:22.500
Take him to the helipad at Bellevue.

180
00:14:23.167 --> 00:14:26.250
-What?
-That's an order from Director Metzger. Go!

181
00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:27.417
Now!

182
00:14:27.667 --> 00:14:28.583
Copy that.

183
00:14:39.583 --> 00:14:41.167
Hey! What...

184
00:14:41.333 --> 00:14:42.750
How did I get up here?

185
00:14:47.083 --> 00:14:50.000
Spider-Man. save me. would you?

186
00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:56.833
Who are you?

187
00:14:58.000 --> 00:14:59.333
You can see me.

188
00:14:59.583 --> 00:15:00.917
Tell me who you are.

189
00:15:02.167 --> 00:15:03.083
You first.

190
00:15:06.250 --> 00:15:08.333
Hey. Hey.

191
00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:15.500
You pushed me out.

192
00:15:16.250 --> 00:15:17.250
Interesting.

193
00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:18.833
What the hell was that?

194
00:15:19.083 --> 00:15:21.167
Did you just try to jump into my mind?

195
00:15:21.333 --> 00:15:24.250
You know. the whole time
you've been chasing me...

196
00:15:25.083 --> 00:15:27.667
you forgot to ask yourself
a very important question.

197
00:15:29.583 --> 00:15:30.917
What's in the tank?

198
00:15:33.000 --> 00:15:34.417
Go! Move.

199
00:15:48.583 --> 00:15:49.583
Spider-Man?

200
00:15:50.833 --> 00:15:51.917
What just happened?

201
00:15:54.917 --> 00:15:55.917
I don't know.

202
00:15:59.333 --> 00:16:00.167
Hey. way to go. Spidey.

203
00:16:00.417 --> 00:16:02.000
You guys okay? You good?

204
00:16:02.167 --> 00:16:05.000
I swear. All the things they said I did.
I don't remember doing any of them.

205
00:16:05.167 --> 00:16:07.167
It's okay. it's okay.
Look. let these people take good care of you.

206
00:16:07.417 --> 00:16:08.167
I would never hurt you.

207
00:16:08.583 --> 00:16:09.417
-Okay.
-I love you. Spider-Man

208
00:16:09.917 --> 00:16:11.250
Yeah. All right. buddy. All right.

209
00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:13.417
-Hey. what do you got?
-Here. get this.

210
00:16:13.667 --> 00:16:15.167
Chopper took Scorpion to Bellevue.

211
00:16:15.417 --> 00:16:17.583
Ten minutes later.
a guard walked him right out the door.

212
00:16:18.167 --> 00:16:18.750
What?

213
00:16:19.167 --> 00:16:20.083
What about the tank?

214
00:16:20.333 --> 00:16:22.833
Stolen from the Damage Control
warehouse in Brooklyn.

215
00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:25.083
Driver was a janitor who worked there.

216
00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:26.167
You got a motive?

217
00:16:26.417 --> 00:16:27.167
Nada.

218
00:16:27.417 --> 00:16:28.417
And no criminal record.

219
00:16:28.583 --> 00:16:30.583
Scorpion must've gotten to her somehow.

220
00:16:31.667 --> 00:16:32.750
Yeah. Maybe.

221
00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:34.917
What do you mean. "maybe"?

222
00:16:35.417 --> 00:16:37.000
I mean. I don't know.

223
00:16:37.833 --> 00:16:39.000
But I know someone that might.

224
00:16:39.250 --> 00:16:40.167
Where you going?

225
00:16:40.417 --> 00:16:41.917
You keep following the leads on Scorpion.

226
00:16:42.167 --> 00:16:43.833
I'm gonna go talk to someone.

227
00:16:59.333 --> 00:17:02.833
Hi. is this 3250 Brighton Beach?

228
00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:08.583
Okay.

229
00:17:09.333 --> 00:17:11.083
I think I know what that means.

230
00:17:16.167 --> 00:17:17.333
Take off your clothes.

231
00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:21.417
What?

232
00:17:21.917 --> 00:17:23.833
You don't wear clothes in the banya.

233
00:17:25.000 --> 00:17:26.333
Ditch the leotard.

234
00:17:27.500 --> 00:17:28.833
This is not a leotard.

235
00:17:29.667 --> 00:17:31.583
Your text said that this was your office.

236
00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:34.500
This is my office.

237
00:17:35.250 --> 00:17:36.250
Get in.

238
00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:38.917
I'm fine. thanks. I'll just...

239
00:17:40.250 --> 00:17:41.583
My office. my rules.

240
00:17:41.833 --> 00:17:45.417
This way you get to enjoy
a nice. relaxing soak.

241
00:17:45.667 --> 00:17:47.833
and I get to see that
you don't have any weapons...

242
00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:49.167
and we both win.

243
00:17:51.417 --> 00:17:52.417
Okay.

244
00:18:01.667 --> 00:18:04.000
Really? What. you never take that off?

245
00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:06.333
No. I... You know. it defeats
the whole anonymous thing.

246
00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:10.917
Even for your girlfriend
or boyfriend or whatever?

247
00:18:11.667 --> 00:18:13.250
There's a lot of conjecture online.

248
00:18:14.083 --> 00:18:16.667
And super graphic artwork. Have you seen?

249
00:18:16.833 --> 00:18:19.417
The one with you
and the ten Mysterios. it's...

250
00:18:19.583 --> 00:18:21.750
I've seen it. I've...

251
00:18:21.917 --> 00:18:23.250
It's hard to unsee. to be honest.

252
00:18:23.500 --> 00:18:25.500
But. look. I don't have anyone.
I just kinda keep to myself.

253
00:18:26.333 --> 00:18:27.833
All by yourself? All the time?

254
00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:29.333
No wonder you're so sad.

255
00:18:29.583 --> 00:18:31.583
-I'm not so sad.
-A little bit.

256
00:18:31.833 --> 00:18:33.667
Could we just talk about
what I came here to talk to you about...

257
00:18:33.833 --> 00:18:35.167
the attack on Damage Control?

